{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For it is a stiff-necked people.</b> And it will sin in any case. And even though when You go with us the sin of the generation will be greater, as You said: רֶגַע אֶחָד אֶעֱלֶה בְקִרְבְּךָ וְכִלִּיתִיךָ (Exodus 33:5), nevertheless it is better for us that You Yourself go with us." "<b>And pardon our iniquity.</b> For with You is pardon, and we shall hope for Your forgiveness, and no angel shall go with us — even though the sin of rebellion would not be so great with him, since with him there is no hope of pardon at all, as You said (Exodus 23:21): כִּי לֹא יִשָּׂא לְפִשְׁעֲכֶם."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:03.081311377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}